.TH CHARBUF_FREE 3 "2023-04-01" "1.0" "lib/charbuf/charbuf_free"
.SH NAME
charbuf_free \- Free a character buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include <lib/charbuf.h>

void charbuf_free(charbuf *b);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcharbuf_free\fR function frees the memory associated with the character buffer \fBb\fR. It releases the memory allocated for the buffer's characters and resets the buffer's state to its initial values.

This function is useful for cleaning up a character buffer when it is no longer needed.
.SH ARGUMENTS
\fBb\fR
The character buffer to free.
.SH RETURN VALUE
None.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcharbuf_free\fR function:
.nf
#include <lib/charbuf.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    charbuf b;
    charbuf_init(&b);
    charbuf_append(&b, "Hello, world!");

    printf("Buffer contents: %s\n", b.chrs);

    charbuf_free(&b);

    return 0;
}
.ne
.fi
